WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
Here are 15 letters from a
gene, read in groups of three.

2
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:10.170
Each time DNA is copied, a rare
error can slip through uncorrected.

3
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:12.690
One base is replaced by another.

4
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:16.580
The sequence is the same length,
but one letter is different.

5
00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.730
The changed DNA is
copied into changed mRNA.

6
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.860
So does the protein always change too?

7
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.570
In this mission, you'll meet the
main ways a sequence can change,

8
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.530
such as swapping a base or removing one.

9
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:35.750
Then you'll delete a single base and watch
what happens to the codons that follow.

10
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.640
Your mission: find out whether changing
one letter in a gene always changes the

11
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:41.480
protein.
